Now I understand the blob persister. Key observations:

1. `recordsFor` builds `model_request_summary` with the detail inline — the detail (per-message block texts) was NOT redacted in the legacy inline path either (only wire dumps are redacted per E1). So the new blob path is consistent with legacy behavior: the detail rides inline unredacted in legacy, now rides into the blob file unredacted. Hmm wait — but session JSONL writes: does the host redact custom records on persist? AGENTS.md said: "hosts persist the hidden `task_ledger` custom record (CLI: ... redacted through the host pipeline — wired through handleAgentEvent's nullable onTaskLedger callback...)". That's for the task ledger. Is there a general session-persist redaction? The redaction hooks: "afterToolCall masks tool results BEFORE session persist, transformContext masks the outgoing context, ... redactPrompt masks user input". So the session content is redacted at the source (tool results, user input) — not at persist. The request detail contains previews of the OUTBOUND context (post-transformContext, so post-redaction). So detail content is redacted at the source. The wire dump is redacted at persist time explicitly (E1). In the new path, `redactWireDump` is passed to the store — the dump IS redacted. Consistent. Good — no security regression there.

  Wait, actually — in the new spill path for the CLI: `redactWireDump: config.redactionPipeline?.redact`. In the app: `_redactionPipeline?.redact`. Both pass redaction. OK.

